    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Scavenger%27s_Guide_to_Droids\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Scavenger's Guide to Droids\">Star Wars Saga Edition Scavenger's Guide to Droids</a></i></p><p><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Magnetic_Feet\" title=\"Magnetic Feet\">Magnetic Feet</a> are a common means of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Locomotion\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Locomotion\">Locomotion</a>. <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droids\" title=\"Droids\">Droids</a> specializing in extra-vehicular activities are often equipped with them. Magnetic Hands function like <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Magnetic_Feet\" title=\"Magnetic Feet\">Magnetic Feet</a>. When used in concert with <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Magnetic_Feet\" title=\"Magnetic Feet\">Magnetic Feet</a>, they provide a +2 bonus to any <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Climb\" title=\"Climb\">Climb</a> checks made while maneuvering around a hull in space, as well as a +5 bonus to <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Defenses\" title=\"Defenses\">Defenses</a> against any attempt to knock the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Droid\">Droid</a> off the hull. When Magnetic Hands are activated, the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Droid\">Droid</a> cannot make attacks or use anything requiring its hands, including Weapons.</p>",
    "source": "Star Wars Saga Edition Scavenger's Guide to Droids",
